"notes": "Modified cash basis governmental funds (fund balances equal cash and CDs); business-type activities on accrual basis, so business_type measure is net position. Governmental receipts/disbursements from the Total Governmental Funds column on p5; beginning cash 1,084,207 is the total fund balance at 9/30/24 (p5) and ending cash 1,029,376 is total assets on the governmental funds balance sheet (p4: cash 904,836 + CDs 116,939 + county treasurer cash 7,601). Transfers net to zero in the total column (General -9,497, Debt Service +9,497), so transfers_in/out are null; shown in detail as other financing. Business-type lines from the proprietary funds total column (p7); no single printed total so reported totals were added (operating revenues + interest income; operating expenses + NDEE fees + interest expense). Statement of cash flows (p8-9) is for the proprietary funds on a non-GAAP-governmental basis; proprietary left null. Balance sheet: government-wide Statement of Net Position (p1) Total column; governmental activities column is modified cash basis. Detail: General Fund recorded from the departmental combining statement Total column (pp14-15), which supersedes the General Fund budget schedule on p10 (budget_final taken from p10 only where the line matches; p10 budget lines are broader for intergovernmental, charges and expenditure functions); the department columns (General, Police, Fire, Sales Tax, Park, Pool, Youth, Library) were not entered separately (8 columns). General Fund expenditures are listed by object across departments, so function is general government except interlocal agreement (public safety), capital outlay and debt service, marked review. Street, Debt Service and Rescue funds from their budgetary comparison schedules (pp11-13); Rescue/Street/Debt Service transfer budget lines with zero actuals omitted. The report has no business-type budget schedules; the Water, Sewer and Trash funds appear only in the proprietary fund statements (pp6-9), and fund-level columns there were not separately entered. Read pages 1-15 of 15"
}
